    "recommendations": "• Trim vegetation along the access drive to maintain clear sight lines for approaching emergency vehicles.\n• Cut back dense vegetation near the detached structure to keep a clear path around all sides for responder movement.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective address numbers visible from the road in both directions.\n• Keep the vehicle parking area clear of parked vehicles that could block emergency access to the main residence.\n• Trim shrubs or trees that block visibility between the main residence and the detached structure.\n• Post visible address or unit markers at the detached structure so responders can identify it as a separate building on arrival.\n• Keep all walkway paths between structures clear of overgrowth to allow responders to move between buildings without obstruction.\n• Identify and mark any secondary access points on the property so responders are aware of all available entry routes."
